{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-109021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{y}{x}={x}^{3}{y}^{3/4}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $Q(x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)={x}^{3},\\,n=\\frac{3}{4}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3/4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{dy}{dx}+\\frac{{y}^{1/4}}{x}={x}^{3}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{1/4}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{4}{y}^{-3/4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3/4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n4\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}\\,z={x}^{3}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{4x}\\,z=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $Q(x)=\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109021" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5fa3099f7f15f92ebd0d5b08cdecb9bc276549c3235d1581cf882b499d0f765"} {"question" "q-109021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-4{x}^{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{3x}"] ["math" "\\frac{1}{4x}"] ["math" "\\frac{4{x}^{3}}{3}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109021" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{{x}^{3}}{4}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "The substitution $z={y}^{m}$ for some real number $m$ transforms the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}-xy=\\frac{\\sqrt[3]{y}}{{x}^{5}}\n$$\n\ninto an equation of the form ${z}^{′}(x)+P(x)z(x)=Q(x).$ What is the function $P(x)?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-x,\\,q(x)={x}^{-5},\\,n=\\frac{1}{3}.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{1/3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-1/3}\\frac{dy}{dx}-x{y}^{2/3}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{2/3}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{2}{3}{y}^{-1/3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-1/3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, equation $(∗)$ can be written as a linear equation in $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-x\\,z=\\frac{1}{{x}^{5}}\n$$\n\nFinally, we write the above equation in standard form, which gives\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{2x}{3}\\,z=\\frac{2}{3{x}^{5}}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=-\\frac{2x}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109024" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5fa3099f7f15f92ebd0d5b08cdecb9bc276549c3235d1581cf882b499d0f765"} {"question" "q-109024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{2x}{3}"] ["math" "-\\frac{3x}{2}"] ["math" "\\frac{2}{3{x}^{5}}"] ["math" "\\frac{3}{x}"] ["math" "\\frac{{x}^{5}}{3}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109024" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-\\frac{2x}{3}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}y={x}^{2}{y}^{-4}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-3{x}^{2},\\,q(x)={x}^{2},\\,n=-4.\n$$\n\nFirst, we multiply the differential equation by ${y}^{4},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{4}\\frac{dy}{dx}-3{x}^{2}{y}^{5}={x}^{2}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{5}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=5{y}^{4}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{4}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{5}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-3{x}^{2}z={x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z=5{x}^{2}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-15{x}^{2},\\,Q(x)=5{x}^{2}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-15{x}^{2})\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z) & ={e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot (5{x}^{2}) \\\\ {e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-15{x}^{2}z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} & =5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}) & =5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 5{x}^{2}{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-5{x}^{3}} & =-\\frac{{e}^{-5{x}^{3}}}{3}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=3{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{5}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{5}=\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}\\,⇒\\,y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109027" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5fa3099f7f15f92ebd0d5b08cdecb9bc276549c3235d1581cf882b499d0f765"} {"question" "q-109027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C-{e}^{3{x}^{2}}}{x}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[3]{\\frac{C{e}^{3{x}^{2}}-1}{2}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C-{e}^{5{x}^{3}}}{{x}^{2}}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}"] ["math" "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{x}-1}{3}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109027" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\sqrt[5]{\\frac{C{e}^{5{x}^{3}}-1}{3}}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}+y=-x{y}^{3}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=1,\\,q(x)=-x,\\,n=3.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{3},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-3}\\frac{dy}{dx}+{y}^{-2}=-x.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-2}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-2{y}^{-3}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-3}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z=-x\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z=2x\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=-2,\\,Q(x)=2x\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (-2)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{-2x}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)={e}^{-2x}$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{-2x}\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z) & ={e}^{-2x}\\cdot (2x) \\\\ {e}^{-2x}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-2z{e}^{-2x} & =2x{e}^{-2x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-2x}) & =2x{e}^{-2x}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(z{e}^{-2x})\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int 2x{e}^{-2x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ z{e}^{-2x} & =-\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{-2x}(2x+1)+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}{2},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=2{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-2}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-2}=\\frac{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}{2}\\,⇒\\,y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109028" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5fa3099f7f15f92ebd0d5b08cdecb9bc276549c3235d1581cf882b499d0f765"} {"question" "q-109028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{2x+1}{C-{e}^{2x}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{2}{C{e}^{x}-2x}"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{1}{C{e}^{x}-1}}"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2x}{C+{e}^{2x}}}"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109028" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{2}{C{e}^{2x}-2x-1}}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109154" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the general solution to the differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{y}{x}=\\sqrt{x}\\,{y}^{2}.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109154" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Notice that our equation is an instance of the Bernoulli differential equation\n\n$$\n\\frac{dy}{dx}+p(x)y=q(x){y}^{n}.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have\n\n$$\np(x)=-\\frac{1}{x},\\,q(x)=\\sqrt{x},\\,n=2.\n$$\n\nFirst, we divide the differential equation by ${y}^{2},$ and we get\n\n$$\n{y}^{-2}\\frac{dy}{dx}-\\frac{1}{x}{y}^{-1}=\\sqrt{x}.\\,\\,(∗)\n$$\n\nThen, we make the substitution\n\n$$\nz={y}^{1-n}={y}^{-1}.\n$$\n\nDifferentiating $z(x)$ using the chain rule, we get \n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}=-{y}^{-2}\\,\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}\\,⟹\\,{y}^{-2}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}.\n$$\n\n \n\nTherefore, the original equation can be written in terms of $z(x)$ as follows:\n\n$$\n-\\,\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}-\\frac{1}{x}z=\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nThis differential equation is linear, so we can use the method of integrating factors. But first, we write the above equation in standard form:\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z=-\\sqrt{x}\n$$\n\nThe above equation is in the standard form\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+P(x)z=Q(x)\n$$\n\nwith\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(x)=\\frac{1}{x},\\,Q(x)=-\\sqrt{x}\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe then compute an integrating factor:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}I(x) & ={e}^{\\int P(x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\int (1/x)\\,\\text{d}x} \\\\  & ={e}^{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x} \\\\  & =x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nMultiplying both sides of the standard form equation by $I(x)=x$ yields\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x\\cdot (\\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+\\frac{1}{x}z) & =x\\cdot (-\\sqrt{x}) \\\\ x\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}z}{\\text{d}x}+z & =-x\\sqrt{x} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz) & =-{x}^{3/2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(xz)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int -{x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ xz & =-\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+{C}_{1} \\\\ z & =\\frac{C-2{x}^{5/2}}{5x},\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C=5{C}_{1}.$\n\nFinally, we determine $y(x)$ by writing $z={y}^{-1}.$ This results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{-1}=\\frac{C-2{x}^{5/2}}{5x}\\,⇒\\,y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109154" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "d5fa3099f7f15f92ebd0d5b08cdecb9bc276549c3235d1581cf882b499d0f765"} {"question" "q-109154" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14052050/state.json" "file_sha256" "5234d91b0202014a85dd166242348b5395de2be2be289d7b9715dba92aa6d2af"} {"question" "q-109154" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "y=\\frac{5x}{C+{x}^{3/2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{5x}{C-2{x}^{5/2}}"] ["math" "y=\\frac{{x}^{2}}{C-5{x}^{5/2}}"] ["math" "y=\\pm \\sqrt{\\frac{x}{C+{x}^{5/2}}}"] ["math" "y={(\\frac{2x}{C-{x}^{3/2}})}^{2}"]] "category" "m